  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "aa9ab4bb-4de0-4dae-9e61-68ab0fe67ea5",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -32,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 1200,
        "content": "## Individual Google forms\n\n### How it works\n\n1. The workflow is manually triggered to start and copies a Google Form template.\n2. The copied form is enhanced with additional details and published for circulation.\n3. A watch is created to monitor responses to the published form.\n4. Upon receiving a new form response, associated webhooks are called to process the data.\n5. Responses are pulled, choices extracted, and a placeholder node handles the extracted information.\n6. Error handling or optional user alerts can be integrated after response processing.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Configure an OAuth 2 client (type \"Web application\" in the Google console\n- [ ] Then in n8n, we need a generic Oauth2 credential with this data: \nGrant Type Authorization Code\nAuthorization URL https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/v2/auth\nAccess Token URL https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token\nClient ID <your client ID>\nClient Secret <your client secret>\nScope(s) - space sep\nhttps://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive https://www.googleapis.com/auth/forms.body https://www.googleapis.com/auth/forms.responses.readonly\n- [ ] Create a template form (G-Form) - and remember the form ID (last part of the URL)\n- [ ] Put the form ID into \"Set params\"\n- [ ] Either edit \"custname\" (customer name) in \"Set params\" as well - or look it up from a G-Sheet et al\n- [ ] In \"Modify form\", adjust the form modification to your needs\n- [ ] Decide whether to use Google watches (then you need to create form-responses topic plus a subscription to the  \"Google watch\" webhook in the Google console. Otherwise, remove the wait node and the \"Google watch\" flow, replace it with a periodic check on whether there's a response\n- [ ] Replace the \"you could send a Mail here\" with sending a mail or slack or whatsapp or ... (or leave it for testing)\n- [ ] Replace the \"do sth with the choice\" (or leave it for testing)\n- [ ] Create a n8n table with form_id and hook_url columns so we can remember which form belongs to which workflow execution.\n\n### Customization\n\nConsider adding more detailed processing based on the form responses extracted."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
